<!-- ===== Overview ===== -->
<section id="overview"><div class="wrap split2">
  <div data-reveal="left">
    <span class="eyebrow">Overview</span>
    <h2 style="font-size:1.9rem;margin:10px 0 14px">About This Box</h2>
    <p style="color:var(--greige-deep)">The Standard Strawberry Box is built around one variety, from one farm, picked at peak ripeness: <b style="color:var(--ink)">Amaou</b> strawberries grown by the Tanaka family at Berry Farm in Yame, Fukuoka. Each fruit is hand-selected, packed at 2–8°C, and flown to Manila under cold chain. Farm to door: 36–48 hours.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="checklist" data-reveal="right">
    <div class="ci"><span class="ck">✓</span><div><b>12 hand-picked berries</b><span>Single harvest day, graded by size and color before packing.</span></div></div>
    <div class="ci"><span class="ck">✓</span><div><b>Net weight ≈ 300 g</b><span>Approximately 25–30 g per berry.</span></div></div>
    <div class="ci"><span class="ck">✓</span><div><b>Brix ≈ 12–14°</b><span>Sweeter than supermarket fruit by a wide margin.</span></div></div>
    <div class="ci"><span class="ck">✓</span><div><b>2–8°C door to door</b><span>Cold chain from Tanaka's greenhouse to your fridge, photo-documented.</span></div></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- ===== The Strawberry: Amaou ===== -->
<section id="strawberry" style="background:var(--cream-2)"><div class="wrap">
  <span class="eyebrow">The Strawberry</span>
  <h2 style="font-size:2rem;margin:10px 0 4px">Amaou</h2>
  <p class="lead-sub">akai (red) · marui (round) · ookii (big) · umai (delicious)</p>
  <div class="split2" style="margin-top:30px">
    <div class="ph soft" data-reveal="left" style="aspect-ratio:1/.82;border-radius:var(--r)"></div>
    <div data-reveal="right">
      <h3 style="font-size:1.2rem;margin-bottom:10px">The variety, briefly</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--greige-deep)">Amaou was developed in Fukuoka in 2005 after a decade of cross-breeding. It's protected — only farms registered with JA Fukuoka can grow and sell it under the name.</p>
      <p style="color:var(--greige-deep);margin-top:12px">Berries average 25–40 g each — twice the size of a typical Tochiotome — with a deep red exterior and a consistent pale-red interior. The flavor is sweetness-forward but balanced: Brix 12–14° vs. 7–9° for most imported strawberries. Floral, candied aroma.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <h3 class="glance-h">At a glance</h3>
  <table class="spec" style="max-width:640px">
    <tr><td>Variety</td><td>Amaou</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Origin</td><td>Fukuoka · 2005</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Berry weight</td><td>25–40 g</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Brix (sweetness)</td><td>12–14°</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Texture</td><td>Firm, juicy, crisp</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Season</td><td>Dec – May</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Peak</td><td>Feb – Mar</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Color (outside)</td><td>Deep red</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Color (inside)</td><td>Consistent pale-red</td></tr>
  </table>
</div></section>

<!-- ===== The Farmer: Tanaka ===== -->
<section id="farmer"><div class="wrap">
  <span class="eyebrow">The Farmer</span>
  <div class="split2" style="margin-top:18px;align-items:start">
    <div class="ph" data-reveal="left" style="aspect-ratio:1/1.05;border-radius:var(--r)"></div>
    <div data-reveal="right">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.9rem;margin-bottom:4px">Tanaka Family · Berry Farm</h2>
      <p class="lead-sub" style="font-style:normal;color:var(--red);font-weight:600;font-size:.82rem;letter-spacing:.04em">YAME, FUKUOKA · PARTNERED SINCE 2021</p>
      <p style="margin:16px 0 0;color:var(--greige-deep)"><b style="color:var(--ink)">A second-generation farm focused on one variety done well.</b></p>
      <p style="color:var(--greige-deep);margin-top:10px">The Tanaka family started Berry Farm in 1992 after Tanaka-san's father switched from rice to strawberries. 2.5 hectares — small enough that every plant is hand-inspected.</p>
      <p style="color:var(--greige-deep);margin-top:10px">They harvest twice a day — early morning and late afternoon — to keep berries from sitting in greenhouse heat. Sugar is measured in the field with a refractometer.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="bigquote" data-reveal style="margin-top:34px">"We don't try to be the biggest farm in Yame. We try to be the one our customers actually remember."<span class="by">— Tanaka-san, Berry Farm</span></div>
  <h3 class="glance-h">Farm facts</h3>
  <table class="spec" style="max-width:640px">
    <tr><td>Farm</td><td>Berry Farm</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Location</td><td>Yame, Fukuoka</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Founded</td><td>1992</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Farm size</td><td>2.5 hectares</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Method</td><td>Greenhouse, hand-picked</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Certification</td><td>JA Fukuoka registered</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Partnered since</td><td>2021</td></tr>
  </table>
  <div class="pd-links" style="margin-top:18px"><a href="#">📍 View Yame, Fukuoka on map →</a><a href="/pages/farmers">Read full farm story →</a></div>
</div></section>

